<task id="163" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Route sweep, Search / RAG / knowledge / Insights surface: close all 15 findings (17 routes) so no route reads, writes, indexes or deletes as the BFF identity on a record, document, chunk or partition the caller chose without a caller-rights decision or an admin policy</title>
    <phase>Session 27, owner round 9: the route authorization sweep (notes/route-authorization-sweep-2026-10-02.md)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-path .cs changes on 17 live BFF routes (tags bff-api, auth, security, testing). Seven of the 15 findings are critical: secure-record content disclosure, cross-tenant index writes and AI grounding poisoning by any signed-in caller.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security work across seven endpoint files with four different id kinds (route id, body id, body subject, index partition), index writes into a shared index, per-row result trimming, and one filter generalization shared with the finance routes. Each route needs its own judgment about which id it acts on.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs (generalized here; consumed by the finance routes), Api/Filters/TenantAuthorizationFilter.cs, Services/Ai/RagService.cs and, if task 167 has landed, tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs, which every round-9 surface task (159-167) also edits. Touches no file under Api/ExternalAccess/** or Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** (CallerRecordAccessProbe is read, not edited).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>130</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, ai, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Owner round 9 (2026-10-03, BINDING): UAC-r2 fixes all 82 sweep findings, critical and high now. This task is the Search / RAG / knowledge / Insights surface: sweep findings #3, #4, #5, #6, #17, #20, #21, #26, #27, #28, #30, #40, #41, #46 and #49 (verified trace for each in the workflow run wf_c2daa097-2f4 journal; summary table in notes/route-authorization-sweep-2026-10-02.md). It TAKES OVER GitHub #1041 ([D-063-1], filed by spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1, labelled defer/next-round), which covered per-document authorization on /api/ai/rag/index, /index/batch and /index-file but missed the cross-tenant halves (the batch checks only the first item's tenant; /index-file has no tenant case at all). Close #1041 from this task's PR. Reviewed and repaired 2026-10-03 (adversarial review against the code; see notes).</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Any signed-in user can today: read the indexed text of any document in the tenant through three search routes; list every indexed file name; make the BFF read any SPE file app-only and index it; inject, overwrite or delete chunks in the tenant knowledge index (and, through a batch, in another tenant's partition); poison or wipe the shared reference grounding index; run Insights playbooks over any matter, project or invoice; and pull an AI summary of any matter, project, event or document. Make every one of these 17 routes either ask Dataverse, as the caller, about the exact record it acts on, or require the SystemAdmin policy, before any read or write. Fail closed. An unknown id and a denied id get the same answer.</prompt>

  <amendments source="main session, 2026-10-03, owner rounds 9-10" binding="true">
    <!-- Read these before step 0. Each overrides anything below that contradicts it. -->
    <amendment>Owner decisions now run to round 10: re-read notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md rounds 9 and 10 on work/unified-access-control-r2 before step 0. They are newer than this POML.</amendment>
    <amendment>Do NOT rename or move FinanceAuthorizationFilter, and do not create a RecordAccessAuthorizationFilter or any other generalized copy of it: reuse it as it is. The rename is follow-up task 170, after the sweep tasks are integrated. Several sweep tasks reuse this filter in parallel, and a move in one of them would conflict with all the others.</amendment>
    <amendment>Task 167 (the every-route guard) runs IN PARALLEL with this task. If RouteAuthorizationGuardTests on your branch has no Pending waiver for your routes (167 not yet landed), do NOT add waivers, ledger entries or Permanent waivers, and do NOT add your files to GovernedFiles. Instead, add a table "Route authorization ledger input" to your task note, with one row per route you changed or deleted: the route key exactly as the guard spells it (VERB /path), the mechanism that now decides (filter, probe or impersonation), the deny test (its fully qualified name, proving a caller without rights is refused), and, for a list whose query runs AS the caller, the words "handler decision: query runs as the caller". The main session records these in 167's ledger at integration. If 167 HAS landed on your branch, follow its ledger contract: delete your Pending waivers and set ResolvedBy and ProofTest in the same diff.</amendment>
    <amendment>Owner round 10 item 1 (BINDING): delete a route when it has NO caller in the repo AND it is NOT in any published API description; fix it otherwise. Search the repo for OpenAPI documents and Copilot or agent plugin manifests (for example *openapi*, ai-plugin*, *manifest*.json, declarativeAgent*) before you decide. List every deletion, with its no-caller and not-published evidence, in the note and the PR. Delete the services, filters and options that only the deleted routes used. Keep the file census count in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests right if a whole endpoint file goes.</amendment>
    <amendment>Impersonation: never assign ServiceClient.CallerId or CallerAADObjectId outside Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseImpersonation.cs (task 160 adds the single SDK entry point there, plus an arch rule). For the Web API, impersonate through DataverseWebApiService's existing impersonateSystemUserId parameter (MSCRMCallerID). It refuses Guid.Empty (task 104).</amendment>
    <amendment>Also in scope (no deferral): the chat Assistant tool path (AssistantToolCallHandler / the insights.query capability) that calls IInsightsAi with a subject the conversation chooses must apply the SAME subject authorization as POST /api/insights/ask.</amendment>
    <amendment>The SystemAdmin policy's scope-substring weakness is fixed by task 165, not here. Do not edit AuthorizationModule.cs.</amendment>
  </amendments>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: BFF endpoint filters (ADR-008), the Spaarke.Core caller-rights seam (AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync, OperationAccessPolicy), the AI document-rights seam (IAiAuthorizationService), Azure AI Search tenant partitioning, ProblemDetails (ADR-019). Fail closed (ADR-003).</role>

  <goal>After this task, for each of the 17 routes listed in the acceptance criteria:
(1) a caller with no rights on the target gets the fail-closed answer, and no Dataverse read, SPE read, AI Search read or write, job submission or playbook run happens for that request;
(2) a caller who holds the required right gets the same behaviour as today, except where an acceptance criterion names a change;
(3) on every record-gated route, the response for a non-existent id and for an id the caller cannot use is identical apart from correlation/trace ids;
(4) every index write lands only in the caller's own tenant partition, taken from the token;
(5) the ten operator routes (knowledge index maintenance, reference indexing, raw chunk injection/deletion) require the SystemAdmin policy;
(6) every search or list result is trimmed to documents the caller can Read;
(7) GitHub #1041 is closed by this task.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 LIVE. Every anchor below was verified against the working tree on 2026-10-03 (branch work/unified-access-control-r2 @ b18a7d321). Line numbers drift: re-verify in step 0.

THE SEVEN FILES AND HOW THEY ARE MAPPED (Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs). `MapRagEndpoints` :263 and `MapKnowledgeBaseEndpoints` :264 are unconditional. `MapAdminKnowledgeEndpoints` :334 is mapped when DocumentIntelligence:Enabled and Analysis:Enabled are both true, which is the shipped default. `MapWorkspaceAiEndpoints` :339, `MapInsightsAskEndpoint` :396, `MapInsightsSearchEndpoint` :403 and `MapInsightsAssistantEndpoint` :412 are unconditional. There is no default or fallback authorization policy in the BFF, so a bare `.RequireAuthorization()` means "signed in".

A. /api/ai/rag (Api/Ai/RagEndpoints.cs). Group :32-34 is a bare `.RequireAuthorization()`. Each route below adds only `.AddTenantAuthorizationFilter()`. `TenantAuthorizationFilter` (Api/Filters/TenantAuthorizationFilter.cs:53-101) only compares the token `tid` with a tenant id it finds in the request, and PASSES THROUGH when it finds none (:76-81). `ExtractTenantId` (:106-158) has cases for RagSearchRequest, KnowledgeDocument, IEnumerable&lt;KnowledgeDocument&gt; (first item ONLY, :121-126), SendToIndexRequest and EmbeddingRequest, then the `?tenantId=` query. It has NO case for FileIndexRequest. RagEndpoints is the filter's only consumer.
  • POST /search :37, handler `Search` :190. Calls `IRagService.SearchAsync(query, options)` with no user. `RagService.SearchAsync` (Services/Ai/RagService.cs:105-111) forwards `user: null`; :142 uses `user ?? options.CallerPrincipal`; with no principal only the public-only privilege filter applies, and privilege_group_ids is never populated by any indexer (project finding A-21; out of scope here), so every chunk passes. `Options.SessionId` (Services/Ai/IRagService.cs:408) routes the search to the shared session-files index filtered only by tenant + that session id, with no ownership check on this route. Results (`RagSearchResult`, IRagService.cs:468-531) carry chunk `Content`, `DocumentId` (documented as the sprk_document id, may be null) and `DocumentName`; there is no parent field on a result. `RagSearchResponse.TotalCount` (:447) is the index count.
  • POST /index :49, handler `IndexDocument` :261, and POST /index/batch :61, handler `IndexDocumentsBatch` :327. The caller supplies the whole `KnowledgeDocument`: `Id` (the index KEY, so merge-or-upload overwrites any existing chunk), `TenantId`, `DocumentId`, `ParentEntity*`, `PrivilegeGroupIds`, `Content`. `RagService.IndexDocumentsBatchAsync` (RagService.cs:549-) takes `tenantId = documentList[0].TenantId` (:559) only to pick the search client and writes every later document with its own TenantId. Under the Shared deployment model all tenants share one physical index partitioned by the tenantId field, so items 2..N of a batch can land in another tenant's partition. The only callers of `IndexDocumentAsync` and of the two routes are this file; `IndexDocumentsBatchAsync` is also called server-side by FileIndexingService.cs:343 and RagIndexingPipeline.cs:174 with server-built documents of one tenant.
  • DELETE /{documentId} :73, handler `DeleteDocument` :375. The route value is a CHUNK key, not a sprk_document id. `RagService.DeleteDocumentAsync` (RagService.cs:711-749) deletes by key "id" alone with no tenantId predicate. Only caller: this route.
  • DELETE /source/{sourceDocumentId} :84, handler `DeleteBySourceDocument` :413. Deletes every chunk whose documentId (sprk_document id) matches, tenant-filtered (RagService.cs:753-). The tenant is the `?tenantId=` query value. No rights check.
  • POST /index-file :105, handler `IndexFile` :497. The file download is OBO (`FileIndexingService.IndexFileAsync`, Services/Ai/FileIndexingService.cs:69), so SPE gates the caller's READ of the file. But the body `TenantId` becomes the AI Search partition verbatim (FileIndexingService.cs:100-113); the body `ParentEntity`, `DocumentId`, `KnowledgeSourceId` and `KnowledgeSourceName` are stamped on every chunk (:312-335; `FileIndexRequest`, Services/Ai/IFileIndexingService.cs:86-); and when `DocumentId` is present the handler stamps sprk_searchindexed / sprk_searchindexedon / sprk_searchindexcompletedon / sprk_searchindexname on that row APP-ONLY (RagEndpoints.cs:561-576, `IDocumentDataverseService.UpdateDocumentAsync`) with no Write check. `DocumentEntity` (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs:333, :651-663) carries GraphDriveId, GraphItemId, MatterId, ProjectId and InvoiceId, and NO work-assignment or event lookup.
  • THE REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION TO COPY is the sibling route in the same file, POST /send-to-index, handler `SendToIndex` :663-, fixed by spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1 task 063 (finding F2): tenant from `TenantResolution.ResolveTenantId(httpContext.User)`; a body TenantId that disagrees is REJECTED 403 `SEND_TO_INDEX_TENANT_MISMATCH` (:701-725, "rejected, never silently corrected"); refuses without caller oid + bearer token (:727-742); per-document Write via `AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync(callerObjectId, "sprk_documents", recordId, callerToken, ct)` and `snapshot.AccessRights.HasFlag(AccessRights.Write)` (:765-769), with the constant `DocumentEntitySetName = "sprk_documents"` (:596); then it reads the row and derives the drive, item and parent from it (Step 1-3b, :808-860). Its tests are tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/SendToIndexAuthorizationContractTests.cs, whose `ProgrammableRecordAccessSource` (:558-) is the access seam to reuse.
  • NOT IN SCOPE in this file (do not change them; task 167 classifies them): POST /embedding, POST /send-to-index, POST /api/ai/rag/enqueue-indexing (RagApiKey policy), and the /admin group (:160-, already `RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin")`).

B. /api/ai/knowledge (Api/Ai/KnowledgeBaseEndpoints.cs). Group :26-28 is a bare `.RequireAuthorization()`. Each route adds `.AddEndpointFilter&lt;AiAuthorizationFilter&gt;()`. `AiAuthorizationFilter` (Api/Filters/AiAuthorizationFilter.cs) only extracts ids from a `DocumentAnalysisRequest`, an `IEnumerable&lt;DocumentAnalysisRequest&gt;` or a non-empty `Guid` argument (:128-152) and calls `next()` when it finds none (:79-82). None of these handlers has such an argument, so on these routes the filter decides nothing. The file's own descriptions call the surface "for evaluation/admin use".
  • GET /indexes/{indexName}/documents :44, handler `GetIndexedDocuments` :167 → `RagService.GetIndexedDocumentsAsync` (RagService.cs:1001-1048): tenant filter only; returns chunk id, documentId, fileName, timestamps and `TotalCount`, pageSize up to 200.
  • DELETE /indexes/{indexName}/documents/{documentId} :58, handler `DeleteIndexedDocument` :253 → `RagService.DeleteIndexedDocumentAsync` (:1054): app-only delete of every chunk of that documentId in the caller's tenant. Its 404 body echoes the documentId and index name (:291-298).
  • POST /indexes/reindex/{documentId} :71, handler `ReindexDocument` :349. Builds a `RagIndexingJobPayload` with `DriveId = request.DriveId` (CALLER-CHOSEN), `ItemId = DocumentId = documentId`, `FileName = request.FileName` and `ReplaceStaleChunks = true` (:384-397), then submits it. `RagIndexingJobHandler` (Services/Jobs/Handlers/RagIndexingJobHandler.cs:131-165) calls `IFileIndexingService.IndexFileAppOnlyAsync`, which downloads with Graph APP-ONLY (Infrastructure/Graph/DriveItemOperations.cs:138-155, `_factory.ForApp()`), so the app reads any drive item the caller names; it then stamps the sprk_document app-only (:203-229). The route conflates the SPE item id with the sprk_document id; with a real sprk_document GUID the ItemId is wrong.
  • POST /test-search :84, handler `TestSearch` :445. Builds `RagSearchOptions` WITHOUT `CallerPrincipal` (:479-486) and returns raw chunk `Content`, DocumentId and DocumentName for up to 20 rows (:490-507). Its count field is `KnowledgeTestSearchResult.ResultCount`. The body `IndexName` is echoed only, never used.
  • GET /indexes/health :31 is NOT a finding (counts only). Do not change it.

C. /api/admin/knowledge (Api/Ai/AdminKnowledgeEndpoints.cs). Group :28-30 is a bare `.RequireAuthorization()` despite the /admin prefix; each route adds the pass-through `AiAuthorizationFilter`. POST /index-references :33 (handler `IndexAllReferences` :79, a full delete-and-re-embed of every knowledge source), POST /index-reference/{knowledgeSourceId} :44 (handler `IndexSingleReference` :107: with body `Content` it writes caller-supplied text into the SHARED system reference index `spaarke-rag-references` under any source id, replacing that source's chunks; without it, it reads any sprk_aiknowledge row app-only through IScopeResolverService), DELETE /index-reference/{knowledgeSourceId} :57 (handler `DeleteReference` :200). The reference index is the T4 grounding source read by RagService, ActionRunner and ReferenceRetrievalService, with TenantId "system" (KnowledgeDocumentSchemaMapper.cs:53), so a write here steers every user's AI answers. `ReferenceIndexingService` is a sealed concrete singleton (Services/Ai/ReferenceIndexingService.cs:45, registered Infrastructure/DI/AiModule.cs:223); its seams are IScopeResolverService, SearchIndexClient and IOpenAiClient.

D. Insights. All three groups are `.RequireAuthorization()` + `.RequireRateLimiting("ai-context")` and no filter.
  • POST /api/insights/ask (Api/Insights/InsightEndpoints.cs:71, handler `Ask` :127). Subject must start "matter:" (:219-230) but the id is not parsed as a GUID. `request.Question` accepts ANY raw playbook GUID (:190; the binding lookup runs only for a non-GUID name). `request.Parameters` are merged into node template expansion and the CALLER'S value wins over the subject-derived one (`InsightsOrchestrator.EnrichParametersFromSubject`, Services/Ai/Insights/InsightsOrchestrator.cs:1101-1137, "Caller-supplied value wins via TryAdd"); the shipped playbooks' templates reference {{matterId}} and {{tenantId}}. `AccessibleScopeHash` (:270, :453-458) is SHA256(tid|oid), a cache key, not a check. LiveFact nodes read the matter APP-ONLY through IGenericEntityService (MatterLiveFactResolver.cs:141; GraphModule.cs:97). Live callers: src/dataverse/forms/sprk_matter/insightCardMount.ts:306-310 and insightWidgetOnLoad.ts:289-293 send `{ question: "matter-health-single", subject: "matter:{id}", parameters: {} }` (a canonical NAME and EMPTY parameters). Test callers that send a raw playbook GUID and/or non-empty parameters: tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Eval/PredictMatterCostEvalHarnessTests.cs:226-228 (raw GUID + golden tuples from tests/Insights/golden/predict-matter-cost.json whose parameter keys are matterId, lookBackYears, currency, matterType), tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/EndToEnd/Phase1SmokeTest.cs:114-117 and :179 (lookBackYears, matterType), tests/integration/contract/Api/Insights/InsightEndpointsContractTests.cs:110 and :400-417 (lookBackYears; raw GUID).
  • POST /api/insights/assistant/query (Api/Insights/InsightsAssistantEndpoint.cs:89, handler `AssistantQuery` :130, streaming `StreamAssistantQuery` :412). Subject via `ISubjectParser` (Services/Insights/LiveFacts/SubjectParser.cs; matter/project/invoice + GUID). No record check before either the playbook path (LiveFact resolvers, app-only) or the RAG path. Live caller: src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/StructuredOutputStreamWidget.tsx (~:389). Test caller: tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests/InsightsToolIntegrationTests.cs:111, :169.
  • POST /api/insights/search (Api/Insights/InsightsSearchEndpoint.cs:95, handler `Search` :120). Subject via `ISubjectParser`; the facade sets ParentEntityType/Id from the subject (:210-219) and `InsightsOrchestrator.SearchAsync` (:905-) sets no index name (the route description says spaarke-insights-index; the code searches the tenant default index), returning names + snippets + an LLM summary. No record check. No in-repo client caller found.

E. POST /api/workspace/ai/summary (Api/Workspace/WorkspaceAiEndpoints.cs:35, handler `HandleAiSummary` :60). Group `.RequireAuthorization()` + `WorkspaceAuthorizationFilter`, which only resolves the oid (it is in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.ClaimOnlyFilters, :1216). `WorkspaceAiService.GenerateAiSummaryAsync` (Services/Workspace/WorkspaceAiService.cs) refuses a type outside `SupportedEntityTypes` (:63-69, OrdinalIgnoreCase: sprk_event, sprk_matter, sprk_project, sprk_document) with InvalidOperationException, which the handler turns into 400 (:176-195). `FetchEntityDescriptionAsync` reads sprk_event / sprk_matter / sprk_project APP-ONLY through IGenericEntityService (:205, :254, :282) and sprk_document through IDocumentDataverseService (:307), then feeds the description to a playbook whose text is returned. A failed matter/project/event read is swallowed into a minimal description and a 200 (:188-197); only a document returns 404 (KeyNotFoundException), and that 404 body echoes the entityType and entityId (WorkspaceAiEndpoints.cs:164-174). No in-repo client caller found; scripts/Deploy-WorkspaceBff.ps1:69 smoke-calls it unauthenticated and expects 401, which is unchanged.

REUSE, NOT NEW MACHINERY (CLAUDE.md §11; read each before using it):
  • Caller rights on one record: `AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync(userId, entitySetName, recordId, callerToken, ct)` (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/AuthorizationService.cs:255-283), OBO RetrievePrincipalAccess, None on every fault and without a token, cached 60 s by CachedAccessDataSource. Consumers: RagEndpoints.SendToIndex :765, SemanticSearchEndpoints.AuthorizeRowsByParentAsync (Api/Ai/SemanticSearchEndpoints.cs:521-, task 070/080), RecordSearchEndpoints.AuthorizeRowsAsync (Api/Ai/RecordSearchEndpoints.cs:246-, task 077).
  • Caller Read on a LIST of documents: `IAiAuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync(user, documentIds, httpContext, ct)` (Services/Ai/IAiAuthorizationService.cs:89; impl Services/Ai/AiAuthorizationService.cs:48-), the AI-domain seam `AiAuthorizationFilter` already uses. It reads the caller's bearer token (Denied without one), asks `IAccessDataSource.GetUserAccessAsync` per id as the caller, requires Read, and returns `AuthorizedDocumentIds` (the permitted subset). It throws ArgumentException on an empty list, and its `Reason` strings contain document ids. This is the per-row trim seam for this task.
  • Which right an operation costs: `OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights(rights, operation)` (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs:320). Existing keys this task uses, adding none: "read" → Read (:163), "write" → Write (:242), "entity.associate_document" → AppendTo (:213).
  • The per-route declaration filter: task 130 turned `FinanceAuthorizationFilter` (Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs, 426 lines) into a general mechanism: `AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter(Func&lt;EndpointFilterInvocationContext, FinanceAuthorizationTargets&gt; resolveTargets, FinanceDenial denial)` (:66-83), `FinanceAuthorizationCheck` (path, entity set, record id, operation, source; :126-), `FinanceAuthorizationTargets.Authorize/Reject` (:170-), paths Document (AuthorizeAsync, sprk_documents) / Record (GetCallerRecordAccessAsync + HasRequiredRights) / Privilege (:102-124), `FinanceDenial.UniformNotFound` and `UniformRecordNotFound(httpContext)` (:87-99, :280-290, reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.record_unavailable`, never echoes the id). A target declaration that throws, declares no check, or names Guid.Empty denies (:309-330, :386-389); a missing oid is a 401 (:299-307). Nothing in that machinery is finance-specific except its name and its entity-set constants (:222-237). It is the shape every record gate in this task needs (body id, body subject, route id → entity set → operation → caller rights → uniform deny).
  • Entity-set resolution: `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:174, internal static) covers matter, project, invoice, workassignment, event, contact, todo (+ the sprk_ forms). The document set is the existing constant "sprk_documents" (RagEndpoints.cs:596, FinanceAuthorizationFilter.DocumentEntitySet :224).
  • Admin policy: `RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin")` (Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs:362-377), already used by RagEndpoints.cs:162, Api/Admin/JobsEndpoints.cs:53 and Api/Admin/MembershipAdminEndpoints.cs:46. ⚠️ VERIFIED at :370-372: the policy also passes when the delegated scope claim (`http://schemas.microsoft.com/identity/claims/scope`) CONTAINS the substring "admin". This task does not change the policy (it is shared); step 0 records whether any scope the BFF exposes contains "admin".
  • Insights playbook binding: `IConsumerRoutingService.GetBindingByPlaybookIdAsync(playbookId, environment, ct)` (Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IConsumerRoutingService.cs:280) returns the ONE best-match enabled binding that targets a playbook (no consumer-type filter), or null; `Binding.ConsumerType` (Services/Ai/PublicContracts/Binding.cs) and `ConsumerTypes.InsightsAsk` = "insights-ask" (ConsumerTypes.cs:203).
  • NOT used here, on purpose: `DataverseImpersonation` (no impersonated query is needed; every decision is a rights question about a known id) and `CallerRecordAccessProbe` (its ~1.6 s not-found backoff, CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs:99-104, lands on every denied row of a result page).

THE ROUTE GUARD. tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs (task 074) governs only the files in `GovernedFiles` (:126-); none of the seven files in scope is governed today. ⚠️ Two facts the executor must not lean on: (1) its `FilterMarker` regex (:1898-1902) CREDITS `.AddTenantAuthorizationFilter()` and `.AddEndpointFilter&lt;AiAuthorizationFilter&gt;()` as a per-route Filter, although neither decides anything on these routes; (2) Rule B (:1107-) passes `AiAuthorizationFilter` because its source references IAiAuthorizationService, a real decision seam, but Rule B cannot see that the filter calls next() when it extracts no ids. So "Rule A passes" proves nothing for these routes. Task 167 (no POML on this branch as of 2026-10-03) extends the guard to every route file, adds Pending waivers owned by 163 for this task's 17 routes and, per owner round 9 item 3, accepts three declarations: a record-level check, an admin policy, or a reasoned waiver.</background>
