  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every route in this task. Fail closed. A missing caller oid, a missing bearer token, an unresolvable Dataverse user, a RetrievePrincipalAccess fault, a seam exception, an unrecognized entity type or a non-GUID id DENIES. There is no app-only fallback on any path. A non-existent id and an id the caller may not use get the IDENTICAL response (status, title, detail, reasonCode, extension keys), and no response body or caller-visible log echoes the requested id or whether the record exists. On every record-gated route in this task that response is the uniform 404 of `UniformRecordNotFound` (reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.record_unavailable`), except where an acceptance criterion names another shape. A missing oid stays the declaration filter's 401 (it does not depend on the record). A token/body TENANT mismatch is a 403: the tenant is in the caller's own token, so it is not an existence oracle.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / project">Scope: every record-level check added. It runs as an ENDPOINT FILTER in the route's own fluent chain, BEFORE the handler, so no Dataverse, SPE, AI Search, job or playbook call happens on a denied request. The only checks allowed inside a handler are: the per-ROW result trims (rag/search, knowledge list, knowledge test-search); the index-file and reindex row comparisons (409s), which need the row read after the filter ran; the /ask playbook-binding and parameters checks (validation of the handler's own inputs); and mapping a post-check KeyNotFoundException or null row to the uniform 404. An endpoint file that does a per-row trim must itself reference `IAiAuthorizationService` or `AuthorizationService`, so the filter/endpoint pair satisfies Rule B (RouteAuthorizationGuardTests :1131-1146).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11 (one declaration filter)">Scope: the record-level filter. Do NOT write a new check loop. Move the domain-neutral machinery of `FinanceAuthorizationFilter` (the Func-declaration overload, the check record, the targets record, the Document/Record/Privilege paths, the Forbidden/UniformNotFound denials and `UniformRecordNotFound`) into `Api/Filters/RecordAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs` under domain-neutral names (`AddRecordAccessAuthorizationFilter`, `RecordAccessCheck`, `RecordAccessTargets`, `RecordAccessDenial`, `RecordAccessCheckPath`). Keep the finance entry points as thin forwards (or update every finance call site in the same change); the finance constants stay on the finance side. The file name must end in "AuthorizationFilter.cs" so RouteAuthorizationGuardTests' Rule B inspects it, and the extension method name must match FilterMarker (`\.Add\w*AuthorizationFilter\s*[&lt;(]`). Every finance contract and arch test stays green with no change of behaviour. The PR carries the three-question justification for the moved type, with grep evidence. If step 0 learns that another round-9 surface task (159-167) has already generalized this filter on master or its branch, STOP and use that one (escalation trigger).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11 (entity sets and seams)">Scope: every entity set and rights seam this task names. Never pluralize a logical name. Use `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` for matter / project / invoice / workassignment / event, and the existing constant "sprk_documents" for documents. Do NOT add an entry to `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` (lockstep invariant with DocumentAssociationMap) or to `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets`, and do NOT declare a new logical-name → entity-set map. Do NOT add an `OperationAccessPolicy` key: "read", "write" and "entity.associate_document" already exist. Do NOT change `IAiAuthorizationService`, `AiAuthorizationService` or `AiAuthorizationFilter`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (operator routes)">Scope: exactly these ten routes: GET /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/{indexName}/documents, DELETE /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/{indexName}/documents/{documentId}, POST /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/reindex/{documentId}, POST /api/ai/knowledge/test-search, POST /api/admin/knowledge/index-references, POST /api/admin/knowledge/index-reference/{knowledgeSourceId}, DELETE /api/admin/knowledge/index-reference/{knowledgeSourceId}, POST /api/ai/rag/index, POST /api/ai/rag/index/batch and DELETE /api/ai/rag/{documentId}. These are operator maintenance surfaces (the knowledge descriptions say "evaluation/admin"; the /index routes take a caller-chosen index KEY, so no per-record check can stop one Write-holder overwriting another document's chunks; DELETE /{documentId} takes a chunk key that is not a Dataverse record; the knowledge DELETE must stay able to remove orphaned chunks of a deleted document). Each carries `RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin")` in its own chain, or on its group for /api/admin/knowledge. On the seven routes in KnowledgeBaseEndpoints.cs and AdminKnowledgeEndpoints.cs, remove `.AddEndpointFilter&lt;AiAuthorizationFilter&gt;()`: it decides nothing on them and would read as a gate. Leave GET /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/health unchanged (signed-in, its AiAuthorizationFilter kept). Do NOT change the SystemAdmin policy itself. The admin policy does not replace the per-row trims or the reindex record check below: an admin's Dataverse rights still decide which documents they see or re-index.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (tenant partition)">Scope: every route here that writes to or deletes from an AI Search index. The partition is the token's tenant (`TenantResolution.ResolveTenantId(httpContext.User)`), never a body or query value. A body or query tenant that disagrees is REJECTED 403 (SendToIndex precedent, RagEndpoints.cs:701-725), never silently corrected. In `TenantAuthorizationFilter.ExtractTenantId` / `InvokeAsync`, add a `FileIndexRequest` case and make the `IEnumerable&lt;KnowledgeDocument&gt;` case reject when ANY item's TenantId is empty or differs from the token (not only the first). Keep the filter's existing pass-through for request types it does not know (send-to-index and others depend on its current shape); each handler in scope checks its own tenant as SendToIndex does, so detaching the filter cannot reopen the hole.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (RagService)">Scope: Services/Ai/RagService.cs, two changes only. (1) `DeleteDocumentAsync` deletes a chunk only when the chunk with that key carries the caller's tenantId (read it first with a query filtered on `id` and `tenantId`); a chunk of another tenant and an absent chunk both return false and delete nothing. Its only caller is DELETE /api/ai/rag/{documentId}. (2) `IndexDocumentsBatchAsync` (both overloads) throws `ArgumentException` BEFORE any write when the documents do not all carry the same TenantId. Do not change any other RagService behaviour, the privilege-group filter, or the session-index routing. Service-level tests substitute `IKnowledgeDeploymentService` / `SearchClient` (virtual members, results built with `SearchModelFactory`, the Spe.Integration.Tests KnowledgeBaseTestFixture precedent at :691-700); no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 9 (list trim)">Scope: POST /api/ai/rag/search, POST /api/ai/knowledge/test-search, GET /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/{indexName}/documents. Results are trimmed to what the caller can read: a row is kept only if its DocumentId parses as a non-empty GUID AND that GUID is in `AuthorizedDocumentIds` returned by ONE call to `IAiAuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync(httpContext.User, distinctParsedIds, httpContext, ct)` for the page. Use that seam, not a copied loop and not a third one. When no row has a usable GUID, do not call it (it throws on an empty list) and return no rows. A row with a null or non-GUID DocumentId is DROPPED, never served. A denied or failed AuthorizeAsync keeps no rows; its `Reason` text is never returned to the caller. A returned count (`RagSearchResponse.TotalCount`, `KnowledgeTestSearchResult.ResultCount`, `KnowledgeIndexedDocumentsResult.TotalCount`) reports the number of rows actually returned, never the untrimmed index count. Do NOT rely on `RagSearchOptions.CallerPrincipal` / privilege groups as the trim: they are never populated (finding A-21, out of scope); but set `CallerPrincipal = httpContext.User` on both rag/search and test-search so the privilege filter sees the caller once groups are stamped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (rag/search request)">Scope: POST /api/ai/rag/search. When `Options.ParentEntityId` is non-empty, the declaration filter checks Read ("read") on the parent: `Options.ParentEntityType` resolved through `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` and the id parsed as a non-empty GUID; an unresolvable type or a non-GUID id denies with the uniform 404. When only `Options.ParentEntityType` is set, there is no parent gate (the per-row trim covers it). A non-empty `Options.SessionId` is refused 400 (no ownership check exists for session files on this route; no in-repo caller sends one). The options passed to `IRagService.SearchAsync` carry TenantId = the token tid.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 9 (writes) / G5">Scope: POST /api/ai/rag/index-file, DELETE /api/ai/rag/source/{sourceDocumentId}, POST /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/reindex/{documentId}. A rights pre-check AS THE CALLER in the declaration filter, then the existing app-only write. (a) index-file, filter: when `DocumentId` is present it must be a non-empty GUID and the caller must hold Write ("write") on sprk_documents(DocumentId); when `ParentEntity` is present the caller must hold AppendTo ("entity.associate_document") on it, resolved through `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (an unresolvable type or non-GUID id denies); both checks run when both are present. index-file, handler: a non-empty `KnowledgeSourceId` or `KnowledgeSourceName` is refused 400 (no caller sends them; they would attribute chunks to a knowledge source's grounding). When `DocumentId` is present, the handler reads the row (`IDocumentDataverseService.GetDocumentAsync`, as SendToIndex Step 1): a null row is the uniform 404; a row without GraphDriveId/GraphItemId, a body DriveId/ItemId that differs from the row's GraphDriveId/GraphItemId, or a body ParentEntity whose (type, id) differs from the row's matter/project/invoice when the row carries one (type compared case-insensitively with the "sprk_" prefix ignored; ids compared as GUIDs) is REFUSED 409 with nothing indexed and nothing stamped. When the row carries a matter/project/invoice, the chunks carry the ROW's parent (built as SendToIndex Step 3); when it carries none (for example a document filed under a work assignment), the chunks carry the body ParentEntity the filter authorized. When both `DocumentId` and `ParentEntity` are absent the file is indexed with no attribution and no Dataverse write, as today. `SearchIndexName` handling is unchanged (it is allow-listed). (b) source delete, filter: Write ("write") on sprk_documents(sourceDocumentId). (c) reindex, filter (after SystemAdmin): Write ("write") on sprk_documents(documentId), because the job stamps that row app-only; handler: read the row; a null row is the uniform 404; the job payload takes DriveId = GraphDriveId, ItemId = GraphItemId, FileName = the row's file name (FileName, else Name), DocumentId = the route id, ParentEntity = the row's matter/project/invoice as SendToIndex Step 3, ReplaceStaleChunks = true; a row without GraphDriveId/GraphItemId, or a non-empty body DriveId that differs from the row's, is refused 409 with no job submitted.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (Insights)">Scope: the three Insights routes. The subject record is authorized for Read ("read"), as the caller, by the declaration filter, before `IInsightsAi` is invoked and before any cache lookup: /ask on sprk_matters(the id after "matter:", which must parse as a non-empty GUID, else 400 from the filter's Reject); /assistant/query and /search on the entity set of `ISubjectParser`'s EntityType via `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (an unparseable subject keeps today's 400). On /assistant/query the check runs before the SSE response is opened, so a denial is a plain ProblemDetails with no SSE frame. On /ask, in the handler: (a) a raw playbook GUID in `question` is accepted only when `IConsumerRoutingService.GetBindingByPlaybookIdAsync` returns an enabled binding whose ConsumerType is `ConsumerTypes.InsightsAsk`; otherwise it gets the same 400 as an unregistered canonical name; (b) a `parameters` key is refused 400 with reasonCode `insights.parameters.not_accepted` when it ends in "id" (case-insensitive: e.g. matterId, projectId, invoiceId, tenantId, userId, documentId), EXCEPT the subject's own key "matterId" with a value equal (as a GUID) to the subject id; every other key (e.g. lookBackYears, currency, matterType) is passed through unchanged. The live callers send `{}`; the eval harness sends matterId equal to its subject plus tuning keys. Do not change `InsightsOrchestrator.EnrichParametersFromSubject` (it is shared with the Assistant path). Read is the required right on the subject: the response discloses facts a reader of the subject can already read, and any write a bound playbook makes is server-derived data about that subject (the task 130 recalculate reasoning). Step 0 verifies that last claim (escalation trigger).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (workspace summary)">Scope: POST /api/workspace/ai/summary. The declaration filter checks Read for exactly the four types the service supports (compared case-insensitively, as `WorkspaceAiService.SupportedEntityTypes` does): sprk_event, sprk_matter, sprk_project → Record path, "read", entity set from `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet`; sprk_document → Document path, "read". An empty EntityId keeps today's 400. An unsupported type makes no rights query and keeps today's 400 (the filter returns no check for it and lets the handler's existing InvalidOperationException path answer; or rejects it with the same 400 body). The handler's `KeyNotFoundException` branch returns the same uniform 404 as the filter's denial (no entityType or entityId in the body), so absent, unreadable and deleted-between-check-and-fetch are indistinguishable for all four types. Keep `WorkspaceAuthorizationFilter` (identity precondition) ahead of the new filter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: RagEndpoints.cs handlers Search, IndexDocument, IndexDocumentsBatch, DeleteDocument, DeleteBySourceDocument and IndexFile. Their 500 responses stop echoing `ex.Message` in `detail` (it can disclose internals and record existence); use a fixed detail and log the exception server-side. Keep the `SdapProblemException` rethrows (400 INDEX_NOT_ALLOWED) and the `FeatureDisabledException` 503s.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (operator scripts)">Scope: scripts/Test-RagSharedModel.ps1 and scripts/Test-RagDedicatedModel.ps1. They index synthetic chunks with a knowledgeSourceId and no documentId, search for them and delete them by chunk key. After this task: (1) the header of each states that it needs a token carrying the SystemAdmin role; (2) each takes a new mandatory `-DocumentId` parameter (a real sprk_document the operator can Read) and stamps it as the synthetic chunks' documentId, so the search steps still find them through the per-row trim; (3) each sends the tenant from the token (no change if it already does). Do not change scripts/load-tests/k6-ai-load-test.js (its /search check accepts 2xx or 401 and it sends no options tenant, so it is already a 400).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (the route guard)">Scope: tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs. If task 167 HAS landed on this branch: make each of the 17 routes pass the guard's per-resource rule as 167 defines it (record-level declaration filter, or the SystemAdmin admin-policy declaration on the ten operator routes), DELETE every Pending waiver whose OwningTask is "163", and keep NoWaiverIsStale and the census green. If task 167 has NOT landed (true at authoring): do NOT edit GovernedFiles, Waivers, FilterMarker or the census in this task; record in the task note, per route, the route key and the mechanism that now gates it, for the main session to reconcile at integration. Either way, never count `.AddTenantAuthorizationFilter()`, `WorkspaceAuthorizationFilter` or `AiAuthorizationFilter` as the per-resource decision for a route in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002 / ADR-038 / project">Scope: whole task. No Dataverse plugins. Tests: no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. Substitute only at module boundaries: IAccessDataSource (reuse `ProgrammableRecordAccessSource`), IAiAuthorizationService, IRagService, IFileIndexingService, IDocumentDataverseService, JobSubmissionService, IInsightsAi, IConsumerRoutingService, IScopeResolverService, and WorkspaceAiService's IGenericEntityService / IDocumentDataverseService. Drive every route through its REAL `Map*Endpoints` in an in-process host (the SendToIndexAuthorizationFixture pattern; for /api/admin/knowledge set DocumentIntelligence:Enabled and Analysis:Enabled). No live Dataverse, SPE or AI Search in CI. Every new guard is proven to bite by seeding: remove it locally, see a named test fail, restore, record it in the task note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement: in BFF (existing routes; no new service; the only new type is the moved declaration filter) citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md. Measure publish size against a FRESH build of origin/master, both sides from a SHORT path (e.g. C:\wt163m / C:\wt163b), both zipped with PowerShell Compress-Archive, equal file counts; report both sizes, the delta and the tool; ceiling 60 MB. `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`: no new HIGH. Run /conflict-check before the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 / project hard gate">Scope: whole task. No scope cuts and nothing deferred; scope found during execution is added here. Before the PR run, in full: the affected tests, the full BFF unit suite (tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests, which compiles tests/integration/contract/**), NetArchTest (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests), and BOTH integration suites with `dotnet test` (tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests and tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests). A build is not a run. Live Dataverse/Azure writes and the live gate are MANUAL and run by the main session; this task never deploys.</constraint>
  </constraints>

