  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Re-verify every anchor in the background (line numbers drift). Then, read-only: (a) inventory every caller of each of the 17 routes in src/, scripts/, src/solutions/CopilotAgent (spaarke-bff-openapi.yaml, spaarke-api-plugin.json, declarativeAgent.json) and tests/, and record it in the task note (at authoring: index-file has 4 source callers — uploadOrchestrator.ts, NextStepsStep.tsx, EntityCreationService.ts via SdapClient IndexFileOperation.ts; /ask 2 form scripts; /assistant/query 1 widget; scripts/Test-RagSharedModel.ps1 and Test-RagDedicatedModel.ps1 call /index, /search and DELETE /{id}; k6-ai-load-test.js calls /search; Deploy-WorkspaceBff.ps1 smoke-calls /api/workspace/ai/summary unauthenticated; no other source caller), and list every ParentEntity type the index-file callers send; (b) check whether task 167 is on this branch; (c) ask the main session whether another round-9 surface task has already generalized FinanceAuthorizationFilter; (d) read every playbook bound as consumer type insights-ask in the repo's playbook definitions (Services/Ai/Insights/Playbooks/*.playbook.json at authoring: matter-health-single and predict-matter-cost, AIAnalysis/Control/Output nodes only) and list each node type that writes to Dataverse and what it writes; (e) record whether any delegated scope the BFF app registration exposes (repo config and infra files only) contains the substring "admin".</step>
    <step order="1">Generalize the declaration filter into Api/Filters/RecordAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs per the constraint; keep finance behaviour identical; run the finance contract tests.</step>
    <step order="2">RAG routes: SystemAdmin on /index, /index/batch, DELETE /{documentId}; per-item tenant checks; record gates on /index-file and DELETE /source/{id}; index-file row comparisons and knowledge-source refusal; rag/search parent gate, SessionId refusal, CallerPrincipal, per-row trim; fixed 500 details. Extend TenantAuthorizationFilter. Change the two RagService methods.</step>
    <step order="3">Knowledge and admin knowledge: SystemAdmin, AiAuthorizationFilter removed from the seven routes, list and test-search trims, reindex record gate and payload derived from the sprk_document row.</step>
    <step order="4">Insights: subject Read gates on all three routes (before the SSE opens on /assistant/query), playbook-GUID binding check and identifier-parameter refusal on /ask.</step>
    <step order="5">Workspace summary: the four-type record gate and the uniform KeyNotFound response.</step>
    <step order="6">Route guard: per the constraint (167 landed or not).</step>
    <step order="7">Tests: the closed set in the acceptance criteria, through the real Map*Endpoints hosts; update the existing tests and the two operator scripts named in relevant-files; seed-prove each guard and record the results.</step>
    <step order="8">Build; run the affected tests, the full BFF unit suite, NetArchTest and BOTH integration suites in full; publish size and CVE checks per CLAUDE.md §10.</step>
    <step order="9">Write notes/task-163-search-rag-knowledge-insights-authorization.md: the caller inventory, the per-route mechanism table (17 rows), the step-0 findings (d) and (e), the seeding proofs, the guard reconciliation state and the manual live gate script for the main session.</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (or the escalation state). Note in the PR that it closes #1041.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A caller found in step 0 (in or outside src: the Copilot agent, a Power Automate flow, a script other than the two operator scripts named above, an evaluation harness) uses one of the ten routes this task puts behind SystemAdmin as a NON-admin user: STOP and report the caller and route. The intended audience is then unclear and is the owner's call; do not widen the route back to "signed in".</trigger>
    <trigger>Step 0(e) finds a delegated scope containing "admin", or it emerges that a principal from a CUSTOMER tenant can hold the Admin/SystemAdmin app role on this BFF (multi-tenant app registration, Model 1 shared tenancy). The shared reference index (TenantId "system") would then be writable across customers by a customer admin. STOP and report; do not edit the SystemAdmin policy in this task.</trigger>
    <trigger>Step 0(d) finds that a playbook bound as insights-ask writes caller-influenced content (not data derived by the server from the subject) to Dataverse, or writes to a record other than the subject. Read on the subject is then the wrong right for /ask and /assistant/query: STOP and name the playbook, the node and the field.</trigger>
    <trigger>A consumer needs /api/ai/rag/search or /api/ai/knowledge/test-search to return chunks with no DocumentId (knowledge-source chunks), which the per-row trim drops: STOP; serving them needs a separate authorization rule for knowledge sources.</trigger>
    <trigger>A consumer sends /api/insights/ask a raw playbook GUID not bound as insights-ask, or an identifier parameter the rule refuses; or a playbook is bound under more than one consumer type so that `GetBindingByPlaybookIdAsync`'s single best match is not the insights-ask row: STOP and report; do not reopen free-form GUIDs or identifier parameters.</trigger>
    <trigger>Step 0(a) finds an index-file caller that sends a ParentEntity type `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` cannot resolve: STOP and report the caller and the type (it would be denied after this task).</trigger>
    <trigger>The live gate shows a Document Upload Wizard or Create-wizard user who can open the parent and created the document is denied on /api/ai/rag/index-file (no Write on the new sprk_document, no AppendTo on the parent, or the new row does not yet carry GraphDriveId/GraphItemId when the wizard calls): STOP and report; do not widen the check or fall back to the body pointers.</trigger>
    <trigger>An internal (non-route) caller of `RagService.IndexDocumentsBatchAsync` legitimately sends documents of more than one tenant in one call: STOP before changing that method.</trigger>
    <trigger>Another round-9 surface task (159-167) has generalized FinanceAuthorizationFilter, or is doing so, on its own branch: STOP and ask the main session which version to build on. Two generalizations would be two access policies.</trigger>
    <trigger>The implementation appears to need a new logical-name → entity-set map, a new entry in `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` or `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets`, a new OperationAccessPolicy key, or a change to `AiAuthorizationFilter` or `IAiAuthorizationService`: STOP and bring the choice to the main session.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`FinanceAuthorizationFilter` (Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs, task 130) already implements per-route (entity set, id, operation) declarations from route, body or query, evaluated as the caller through `AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync` + `OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights`, with a uniform 404. `IAiAuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync` (Services/Ai/AiAuthorizationService.cs) already answers "which of these documents may the caller Read". `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` (task 076) reads only the fixed route keys {entityLogicalName}/{recordId}. `EntityAccessFilter` reads an Office SaveRequest body and passes through without a target. `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter` reads only a SemanticSearchRequest. `AiAuthorizationFilter` reads only DocumentAnalysisRequest or Guid arguments and passes through otherwise. The SystemAdmin policy exists (AuthorizationModule.cs:362).</existing>
    <extension>Yes. No new service, no new policy, no new OperationAccessPolicy key and no new entity-set map. The only new type is the domain-neutral home of FinanceAuthorizationFilter's existing declaration machinery (moved, not duplicated), because putting "Finance" filters on RAG, Insights and Workspace routes would misdescribe them and the next surface task would copy the misdescription. The per-row trims call the existing IAiAuthorizationService instead of copying a loop. RagService gets two narrow guards inside existing methods. TenantAuthorizationFilter gets one new case and one corrected case.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Any signed-in user reads the indexed text of documents under secure matters (rag/search, test-search, insights/search), lists their file names (knowledge list), makes the app read any SPE file and index it (reindex), injects or overwrites chunks in their tenant's index and in another tenant's partition (index, index/batch, index-file), deletes any document's chunks (three delete routes), poisons or wipes the shared AI grounding index (admin knowledge), runs Insights playbooks over any matter, project or invoice (ask, assistant/query), and pulls an AI summary of any matter, project, event or document (workspace summary).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

