  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/ai/rag/search (finding #5): (a) a caller holding Read on none of the returned documents gets 200 with an EMPTY result list and TotalCount 0; (b) rows are kept only when DocumentId is a non-empty GUID that `IAiAuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync` returns as authorized; a row with a null or non-GUID DocumentId is never returned, and when no row has a GUID the seam is not called; TotalCount equals the number of rows returned; (c) a caller with Read on every document gets the same rows as before the change; (d) with Options.ParentEntityId set, a parent that is non-existent, of an unrecognized type, non-GUID or not readable by the caller gets the uniform 404 and `IRagService.SearchAsync` is not invoked; (e) a non-empty Options.SessionId gets 400 and no search runs; (f) the options passed to `IRagService.SearchAsync` carry TenantId = the token tid and CallerPrincipal = the request's user (asserted on the substituted seam); (g) a body Options.TenantId different from the token tid still gets 403.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/ai/rag/index and POST /api/ai/rag/index/batch (finding #6): a signed-in caller without the SystemAdmin role gets 403 and `IRagService` is not invoked; for a SystemAdmin caller, a document whose TenantId differs from the token tid gets 403 with nothing written, including when ONLY a document after the first differs or is empty (batch); `RagService.IndexDocumentsBatchAsync` throws ArgumentException before any write for a list whose documents carry more than one TenantId (service-level test, both overloads).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DELETE /api/ai/rag/{documentId} (finding #30): a caller without SystemAdmin gets 403 and `IRagService.DeleteDocumentAsync` is not invoked; a query tenantId different from the token tid gets 403; for a SystemAdmin caller, `RagService.DeleteDocumentAsync` deletes nothing and returns false when the chunk with that key belongs to another tenant, and the route's response for that key is identical to its response for a chunk key that does not exist (service-level test plus route test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DELETE /api/ai/rag/source/{sourceDocumentId} (finding #30): a caller without Write on sprk_documents(sourceDocumentId), a non-existent id and a non-GUID id all get the identical uniform 404 and `IRagService.DeleteBySourceDocumentAsync` is not invoked; a caller with Write gets today's 200; the tenant passed to the service is the token tid, and a query tenantId different from it gets 403.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/ai/rag/index-file (finding #4, #1041): (a) a body TenantId different from the token tid gets 403 and nothing is indexed — proven separately via TenantAuthorizationFilter's new FileIndexRequest case and via the handler's own check (filter detached in a seeding run); the partition passed to `IFileIndexingService` is the token tid; (b) with DocumentId present: a caller without Write on sprk_documents(DocumentId), a non-existent DocumentId and a non-GUID DocumentId all get the identical uniform 404, and neither `IFileIndexingService.IndexFileAsync` nor `IDocumentDataverseService.UpdateDocumentAsync` is invoked; (c) with ParentEntity present: a caller without AppendTo on the parent, and a parent of an unrecognized type, get the uniform 404 and nothing is indexed; (d) with DocumentId present and the rights held: a row with no GraphDriveId/GraphItemId, a body DriveId or ItemId different from the row's, and a body ParentEntity different from the row's matter/project/invoice each get 409 with nothing indexed and nothing stamped; when the row carries a matter/project/invoice the chunks carry the row's parent; when it carries none and the body names a work assignment the caller can AppendTo, the chunks carry the body parent; (e) a non-empty KnowledgeSourceId or KnowledgeSourceName gets 400 and nothing is indexed; (f) with DocumentId and ParentEntity both absent the file is indexed with no Dataverse write; (g) a request in the exact shape uploadOrchestrator.ts sends (driveId, itemId, fileName, tenantId, documentId, parentEntity {entityType "matter"}, searchIndexName) from a caller with Write on the document and AppendTo on the matter gets 200 and the stamp is written; the shape EntityCreationService.ts sends with no documentId and a parentEntity gets 200 with no Dataverse write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/{indexName}/documents (finding #26): a caller without SystemAdmin gets 403 and `IRagService.GetIndexedDocumentsAsync` is not invoked; for a SystemAdmin caller, only rows whose documentId is a GUID that `IAiAuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync` authorizes are returned, and TotalCount equals the number returned.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DELETE /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/{indexName}/documents/{documentId} (finding #27): a caller without SystemAdmin gets 403 and `IRagService.DeleteIndexedDocumentAsync` is not invoked; a SystemAdmin caller gets today's behaviour.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/reindex/{documentId} (finding #28): a caller without SystemAdmin gets 403 and no job is submitted; for a SystemAdmin caller, a caller without Write on sprk_documents(documentId), a non-GUID documentId and a non-existent documentId all get the identical uniform 404 and no job; the submitted job's DriveId, ItemId and FileName come from the sprk_document row (GraphDriveId, GraphItemId, file name) and DocumentId is the route id; a non-empty body DriveId that differs from the row's gets 409 and no job; a row with no GraphDriveId or GraphItemId gets 409 and no job; ReplaceStaleChunks stays true (KnowledgeBaseReindexReplaceStaleChunksContractTests still asserts it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/ai/knowledge/test-search (finding #3): a caller without SystemAdmin gets 403 and no search runs; for a SystemAdmin caller, the options carry CallerPrincipal = the request's user, the returned rows are only those whose DocumentId is a GUID that `IAiAuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync` authorizes, and ResultCount equals the number returned.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seven operator routes in /api/ai/knowledge and /api/admin/knowledge no longer carry `AiAuthorizationFilter`; each carries `RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin")` in its own chain or its group's; GET /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/health is unchanged.</criterion>
