  <notes>Owner round 9 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md, BINDING) is the mandate and fix pattern: reads decided by the caller's own Dataverse rights; writes pre-checked as the user then written app-only only where needed; lists trimmed; fail closed with unknown = denied. Fifteen findings, seventeen route keys: POST /api/ai/rag/search, POST /api/ai/rag/index, POST /api/ai/rag/index/batch, DELETE /api/ai/rag/{documentId}, DELETE /api/ai/rag/source/{sourceDocumentId}, POST /api/ai/rag/index-file, GET /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/{indexName}/documents, DELETE /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/{indexName}/documents/{documentId}, POST /api/ai/knowledge/indexes/reindex/{documentId}, POST /api/ai/knowledge/test-search, POST /api/admin/knowledge/index-references, POST /api/admin/knowledge/index-reference/{knowledgeSourceId}, DELETE /api/admin/knowledge/index-reference/{knowledgeSourceId}, POST /api/insights/ask, POST /api/insights/assistant/query, POST /api/insights/search, POST /api/workspace/ai/summary. Takes over GitHub #1041. Out of scope: finding A-21 (privilege groups never stamped; project CLAUDE.md "Out of scope"), POST /api/ai/rag/enqueue-indexing and /embedding (task 167 classifies them), the SystemAdmin policy's scope-substring weakness (verified at AuthorizationModule.cs:370-372; this task only reports what step 0(e) finds), and internal (non-route) callers of IInsightsAi such as the chat Assistant tool path. Known pre-existing break, unchanged by this task: NextStepsStep.tsx:697 posts to /index-file with no tenantId and already gets 400. Known pre-existing gap, unchanged: the matter-form insight scripts call fetch with `credentials:"include"` and no bearer token, so live-gate item (e) is conditional. Caching: IAiAuthorizationService and AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync go through CachedAccessDataSource, which caches None for 60 s (defect C12, task 132), so a newly granted reader may see the 404 or a trimmed list for up to a minute. Review repairs 2026-10-03: per-row trims moved onto the existing IAiAuthorizationService seam; index-file parent rule made to accept a work-assignment parent the row cannot express; reindex given a caller Write check (it stamps the row app-only); /ask parameter rule narrowed to identifier keys so the eval harness tuning keys survive; knowledge-source fields refused on index-file; operator scripts and the eval/smoke tests added to scope; the SystemAdmin scope-substring claim marked verified.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute; Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check are mandatory (FULL).</protocol>
    <result date="2026-10-03" branch="task/uac-r2-163" base="91a1c1c83">
      <summary>Code complete; all 17 route keys closed. NINE DELETED under the binding owner round 10 item 1 amendment (no caller in the repo, in no published API description): POST /api/ai/rag/index/batch, DELETE /api/ai/rag/source/{sourceDocumentId}, the four /api/ai/knowledge maintenance routes (list, delete, reindex, test-search) and all three /api/admin/knowledge routes (whole AdminKnowledgeEndpoints.cs, with ReferenceIndexingService, ISchemaMapper and KnowledgeDocumentSchemaMapper, its only dependents). EIGHT FIXED: rag/search (per-row trim through one IAiAuthorizationService call per page, parent Read gate, SessionId refused, token tenant, CallerPrincipal set), rag/index and DELETE /rag/{documentId} (SystemAdmin, token-tenant partition, tenant-bound RagService delete), rag/index-file (#1041: FileIndexRequest tenant case + handler check; Write on the named document and AppendTo on the named parent as the caller; row comparisons 409; knowledge-source fields 400), insights ask / assistant/query / search (subject Read as the caller before IInsightsAi; /ask raw GUIDs only when bound insights-ask, identifier parameters refused, canonical subject passed on), workspace/ai/summary (Read on the named record; KeyNotFound is the same uniform 404). ESCALATED (unanswered trigger 3): matter-health-single persists synthesized text to sprk_matter.sprk_performancesummary app-only and parameters.currentGrade reaches its prompt, so whether Read suffices for /ask is the owner's call; Read is implemented as the floor (note section 3.4, options A/B/C, C recommended).</summary>
      <step0>(a) caller inventory in note 1.2: the knowledge, admin-knowledge, index/batch and source-delete routes have no caller and are in no published API description (CopilotAgent OpenAPI has 36 paths, none of these); /assistant/query is the subject of the published E3 tool-call contract; /insights/search is published in the Insights maker guides (kept: judgment, note 2.3); workspace summary has the deploy smoke caller; every index-file ParentEntity type resolves through EntityAccessFilter. (b) 167 not on this branch. (c) answered by the amendment: FinanceAuthorizationFilter reused unchanged, no RecordAccessAuthorizationFilter. (d) matter-health-single persistEnvelope (UpdateRecord) writes sprk_matter.sprk_performancesummary; predict-matter-cost writes nothing and has no insights-ask binding in the seed. (e) live read-only: no delegated scope contains "admin"; the app is AzureADMultipleOrgs with one User-assignable app role "Admin" (reported for task 165; the shared reference-index write path is deleted).</step0>
      <mechanisms>Filters: FinanceAuthorizationFilter declarations (UniformNotFound) on ask, assistant/query, insights/search, workspace summary; AddTargetedRecordAuthorizationFilter (private, RagEndpoints.cs) runs the same filter only when rag/search names a parent or index-file names a document/parent. Admin policy: RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin") on rag/index and DELETE rag/{documentId}. Handler decision: rag/search per-row trim (IAiAuthorizationService). Tenant: TenantAuthorizationFilter FileIndexRequest case + every-item batch check; each writing handler re-checks against TenantResolution.ResolveTenantId. RagService: DeleteDocumentAsync deletes only a chunk with that key in the caller's tenant; IndexDocumentsBatchAsync refuses a mixed-tenant list before any embedding or write. ADR-019: fixed 500 details in RagEndpoints.</mechanisms>
